    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1153">

                <pb facs="1170" n="1160" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11–449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Strong</hi>)<anchor n="96" xml:id="d1153-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-05T17:00:00-05:00">November 5, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>TelCan 745. Re Taipei’s 660, Nov 4, rptd Chungking 216, Hong Kong 66, and
                        AirAtt<anchor n="97" xml:id="d1153-f2"/> Taipei’s Oil, Nov 5,<anchor n="98"
                        xml:id="d1153-f3"/> being rptd Chungking Hong Kong Shanghai.</p>
                <p>You are instructed seek appointment with FonMin<anchor n="99" xml:id="d1153-f4"/>
                    and inform him orally of receipt this info from CAF. You shld state US Govt
                    trusts that this info inaccurate or that it represents attitude irresponsible
                    elements Taipei and not considered view Chi Govt, and you shld request
                    assurances this regard. You shld add that US Govt wld view with serious concern
                    any declared intention Chi Govt bomb US vessels either on high seas (Formosan
                    Straits) or within Chi terr waters, whether those waters controlled by Natl Govt
                    or Chi Commies; that US Govt wld consider any unprovoked attack on US shipping
                    as act of utmost gravity and one not in consonance with relations friendly
                    nations.</p>
                <p>ConGen Taipei shld orally inform Chen Cheng<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1153-f5"/>
                    above representations being made Chungking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1153-f1" n="96" type="source" xml:id="d1153-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Consul General at Taipei as No. 434.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1153-f2" n="97" xml:id="d1153-f2-content">
                <p>Air Attaché.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1153-f3" n="98" xml:id="d1153-f3-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1153-f4" n="99" xml:id="d1153-f4-content">
                <p>George Kung-chao Yeh.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1153-f5" n="1" xml:id="d1153-f5-content">
                <p>Governor of Taiwan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
